  "doc": "A tree of southern swamps and blackwater rivers: a deciduous conifer with a swollen, buttressed base standing in water, woody knees rising from its roots, horizontal limbs hung with Spanish moss, feathery needles that turn rust-orange in fall and drop. Young trees are narrow cones; old ones flatten on top. Wood: baldcypress (Wood Handbook, green).",
